<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Food Supply Crisis Report"
  description="Privacy policy for Food Supply Crisis Report covering analytics, advertising, cookies, external services and website communications."
>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Last updated: October 4, 2026.</strong></p>
    <p>Food Supply Crisis Report publishes evidence-led information about food supply, food prices, food security, climate, water, fertilizer and related topics. This policy explains how the website may use analytics, advertising and information you provide through available contact channels.</p>

    <h2>Information collected</h2>
    <p>The site is built as a static publication. We do not require an account or login to read articles. Information may still be processed by third-party services used to operate the site, measure traffic or receive communications.</p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>When Google Analytics 4 is enabled, it may collect standard website measurement information such as page views, approximate device or browser information and traffic-source data. Analytics is used to understand aggregate site usage and improve the publication.</p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>Advertising is currently disabled on the site. If advertising is introduced later, this policy will be updated before those services are enabled to describe the relevant providers, technologies and choices.

    <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>Cookies or similar technologies may be used by analytics and external services. Your browser may provide controls for managing cookies. Where applicable, additional consent or disclosure mechanisms may be required by local law and the relevant service configuration.</p>

    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>Articles and pages may link to government agencies, research organizations, news outlets and other external websites. Those sites operate under their own privacy policies and terms.</p>

    <h2>Information you send us</h2>
    <p>When you use an available contact or correction channel, information you choose to provide may be used to review the request, respond to you and maintain an editorial record where appropriate. Do not send sensitive personal information through an ordinary correction request.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>This policy may be updated when the website's analytics, advertising, contact or data practices change. The latest version will be posted on this page with its update date.</p>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
